issing. The findings only confirm the financial value of the agreement, its location, and its timing [S2][S3][S5][S6][S7]. There are no conflicting results regarding capacity numbers; rather, there is a consistent absence of this information across all cited documents.\n\nUncertainty:\nThe research could not determine Amkor's current maximum advanced-packaging capacity for NVIDIA chips nor its projected annual growth rate. The available evidence confirms the existence and value of the partnership but lacks the specific production volume data required to answer how fast that capacity can grow.", "audit": {"citations": 7, "unknown_citations": [], "cited_pages": 2, "cited_snippets": 5, "cited_domains": ["bizjournals.com", "en.sedaily.com", "ir.amkor.com", "reuters.com", "seadivi.asia", "secure.businesswire.com", "thebuildout.ai"], "numbers": 2, "numbers_in_cited_source": 0, "numbers_elsewhere_in_evidence": 2, "numbers_ungrounded": 0, "ungrounded_examples": [], "sentences_with_figures_but_no_citation": 1, "numeric_grounding": 0.0}, "run_dir": "experiments/results/baseline_v1/runs/20261011-011439_baseline_which-supplier-s-advanced-packaging-capacity-mos", "answered": true, "facts_found": [], "facts_missed": ["the supplier is TSMC", "the packaging technology is CoWoS"], "fact_recall": 0.0, "fact_recall_in_evidence": 0.5, "coverage_missed": [], "coverage": 1.0, "grounding": 1.0, "quality": 0.667, "cites_authoritative_source": true, "ref_model_seconds": 170.3, "observed_gen_tps": 22.3}
